# apps/api — local-developer environment variables.
#
# Substantive Fastify route + module wiring lands in downstream Epic 1
# stories. At Story 1.2 the only documented env-var is the database
# connection path.

# === Database connection ===
#
# Production paths resolve via GCP Secret Manager (architecture §5.9 line
# 3320-3327) — DO NOT set DATABASE_URL in any non-local execution context.
# Local-developer access uses the Cloud SQL Auth Proxy + a local
# DATABASE_URL pointing at the proxy's loopback socket.
#
# Local-dev steps (see packages/domain/README.md for full detail):
#
#   1. Install the proxy:    https://cloud.google.com/sql/docs/postgres/sql-proxy
#   2. Authenticate:         gcloud auth application-default login
#   3. Start the proxy:      cloud-sql-proxy --port=5432 \
#                              twt-dev:asia-south1:twt-dev-postgres &
#   4. Set DATABASE_URL:     postgresql://twt_dev_app:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/twt_dev?sslmode=disable
#   5. Run migrations once:  pnpm db:migrate
#   6. Start the API:        pnpm --filter @twt/api dev
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://twt_dev_app:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/twt_dev?sslmode=disable
